     "sup": true,
     "group": "in",
     "text": "The water outside the bag has the higher water potential. There is a net movement of water into the bag by osmosis, so the bag swells and becomes firm. Once the bag is full and firm, the stretched tubing presses on the solution inside, and then as many water molecules leave the bag as enter it."
